sase-1nf[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Fix the athena/apollo audit findings the triage ranked worth fixing[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Apollo's and athena's managed-tmp reaper reclaims dead scratch even[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]with SSH sessions open and read-only test trees present, and its [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]jobs report failures truthfully. Agent cleanup works while any [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]agent waits on an epic. `sase doctor -j` always prints JSON. [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Artifact-link projection converges past missing or foreign bead [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]endpoints. Agent-hood publication drains its quarantine backlog [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]through measured fixes and bounded retries. The TUI's multi-second [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]GC freezes are attributed and fixed against sase-1f3's targets. [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Task beads sase-1bw, sase-1ne, sase-1nb, sase-1na, sase-1c5, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]sase-1f4, sase-1f3, sase-10x, and sase-1nc are closed with [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]evidence, and the stalled epic sase-11o is superseded.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]14[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]athena_apollo_audit_fixes.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/athena_apollo_audit_fixes.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1nf[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1nf/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase-core reaper removes read-only trees and exempts [/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]system-service sessions[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]reap-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]reap-core: in sase-core, make managed-tmp removal repair owner write [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]permission inside the candidate tree and retry once, add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]system-service ancestry exemption to the launch-scratch liveness [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]observer, and surface the blocking process in dead-launch and pressure [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]skip reasons.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Truthful managed_tmp_reap and disk_pressure jobs on the new [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]core[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]reap-sase[dim] · [dim][/dim]after reap-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]reap-sase: move the core pin, log removal errors and blocking processes,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]make managed_tmp_reap report check_error on removal failures, make [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]disk_pressure reap before notifying with an explicit status table, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]update the housekeeping and runtime docs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob-cli tests stop leaking read-only vault fixtures[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]bobcli-vault[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bobcli-vault: in the bob-cli repo, restore write permission after the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]read-only completion test locks its fixture vault, and make the test [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]TempDir removal repair owner write permission inside its own tree.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Lossless EpicFollowView encoding for bundles and cleanup [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]payloads[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]cleanup-encoding[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cleanup-encoding: encode wait_epic_follows explicitly in the shared [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent bundle encoder, decode it back into EpicFollowView, guard against [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the next non-JSON field, and make the cleanup test harness round-trip [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]payloads through JSON. Closes sase-1nb.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase doctor survives unbound macro templates[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]doctor-macros[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]doctor-macros: expand macros with raise_on_error in the model-macro [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]check, skip parameterized macros explicitly while still reporting [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]concrete broken presets, and make the diagnostics registry convert [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]SystemExit into an ERROR check. Closes sase-1na.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase-core partial bead link projection and per-endpoint [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]receipts[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]links-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]links-core: add a skip mode to bead link projections that applies valid [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]requests and reports missing holders per request, and extend the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]artifact-link publication receipt with per-endpoint outcomes and an [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]acknowledged, parked, or pending disposition.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Route, isolate, and commit artifact-link bead endpoints per [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]operation[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]links-project[dim] · [dim][/dim]after links-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]links-project: move the core pin, classify every bead endpoint by owning[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]store, project only local endpoints in skip mode, commit chunks that [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]already applied when a later chunk fails, and give each operation its [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]own endpoint evidence.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Parked endpoints leave the retry loop and the sweep converges[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]links-converge[dim] · [dim][/dim]after links-project[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]links-converge: move parked operations into a replayable parked ledger, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]make outbox appends idempotent, sweep per document, report projection [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]failures and parked counts in the artifact_link_backfill job status, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]expose parked counts in doctor.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Instrument and measure agent-hood publication drains[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]pub-measure[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pub-measure: supersede the stalled sase-11o epic, add permanent stage [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]timing, a sync-lock holder record, and richer outbox doctor output, then[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]measure one representative drain on athena and inspect apollo's wedged [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]clone read-only, and publish the findings as a research report.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fix the measured publication failure causes[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]pub-fix[dim] · [dim][/dim]after pub-measure[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pub-fix: plan from the measurement report, then stop repo-wide failures [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]from charging every request's attempt budget, harden the drain timeout, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bound the measured per-drain cost, resolve the stale-commit conflicts, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and add a bounded retry selector.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  11 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Drain the publication backlog on athena and apollo in bounded[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n       [bold #D7AFFF]batches[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]pub-recover[dim] · [dim][/dim]after pub-fix[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pub-recover: on both hosts, back up unique unpublished content, retry [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]quarantined requests in bounded batches while verifying remote [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]publication and a falling backlog, confirm new agents publish, and close[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase-10x.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  12 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]GC attribution telemetry and an acceptance-grade freeze [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n       [bold #D7AFFF]report[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]gc-instrument[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gc-instrument: fix tui_freeze_report's startup-row, rotation, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]trigger handling and add an acceptance mode, add collection start, input[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]age, fault deltas, source revision, and allocator stats to TUI [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]telemetry, and add an opt-in GC census. Closes sase-1f4.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  13 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Measure and attribute the TUI GC freezes on restarted TUIs[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]gc-measure[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gc-instrument[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gc-measure: have the user restart their TUIs onto the instrumented code,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture busy-hour and 4-hour windows on both Python versions, attribute [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]garbage and survivors by type and producer, correlate long pauses with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]swap, and report against sase-1f3's targets.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  14 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fix the measured GC freeze causes[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]gc-fix[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gc-measure[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gc-fix: plan from the measurement report, reduce allocation and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]retention at the measured producers before touching collector policy, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]resolve the backstop quiet-window conflict, and prove sase-1f3's targets[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]on restarted TUIs. Closes sase-1nc.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-1nf","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-1nf.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-ee3a6d411715e6cd93ef93b284be6b5b","started_at":"2026-10-20T17:39:31.546781+00:00","state":"active"}],"schema_version":2,"structural_ancestors":["bbugyi200.athena.sase-1nf","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1nf.1","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1nf.10","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1nf.11","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1nf.12","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1nf.13","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1nf.14","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1nf.2","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1nf.3","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1nf.4","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1nf.5","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1nf.6","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1nf.7","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1nf.8","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1nf.9","bbugyi200.athena.sase-1nf.land"]}
